# ga-usb-port-allowlist — USB port paths authorized on this board, one per line,
# as <host controller>:<port chain>. With usbcore.authorized_default=0 (set in
# uboot-boot.ush) a device binds to a driver only if /usr/libexec/ga-usb-authorize
# finds it here or in /usr/share/ga-usb-allowlist (VID:PID).
#
# These are the board's internal devices behind the on-board hub. A port path
# is fixed by the board wiring: plugging an adapter into an external port can
# not give it one of these names, whatever IDs the adapter reports. External
# ports stay closed; an external device needs a VID:PID declaration.
#
# NOT the sysfs name (3-1.2): its bus number follows controller probe order and
# moves between boots (Odoo #2189). ff5c0000.usb is the EHCI controller the hub
# hangs off (its OHCI companion ff5d0000.usb and the xHCI are other controllers).
#
#   ff5c0000.usb:1     the on-board hub
#   ff5c0000.usb:1.1   the cellular modem
#   ff5c0000.usb:1.2   on-board serial radio
#   ff5c0000.usb:1.3   on-board serial radio
ff5c0000.usb:1
ff5c0000.usb:1.1
ff5c0000.usb:1.2
ff5c0000.usb:1.3
